      "Ultimately, financial engineering is neither an inherently destructive alchemy nor a substitute for industrial excellence. When subordinated to real operational investment and governed with transparency, it is a vital catalyst for capital formation; when detached from underlying productive cash flows, it inevitably degenerates into fragile financial speculation."
