"texte": [
"MACRO-HISTORICAL & INSTITUTIONAL POLITICAL ECONOMY ESSAY — EUROPEAN REVIEW OF GLOBAL ECONOMIC GOVERNANCE AND CAPITALISM STUDIES. Over the past two centuries, capitalism has demonstrated an extraordinary institutional capacity to reinvent itself in response to technological revolutions, social upheavals, and geopolitical realignments—evolving from nineteenth-century laissez-faire industrial capitalism through post-war Keynesian welfare capitalism to the hyper-globalised, shareholder-centric neoliberal model that dominated the late twentieth century.",
"Today, at the end of the first quarter of the twenty-first century, global capitalism is undergoing another profound structural metamorphosis driven by four converging forces: deep yet weaponised global economic interdependence, the rise of intangible digital and artificial-intelligence platforms, the existential imperative of ecological decarbonisation, and the assertive return of state industrial policy.",
