      "The sharpest commercial and legal friction centres on 'Standard-Essential Patents (SEPs)'—patents protecting technical inventions indispensable to implementing global interoperability standards such as 5G telecommunications, Wi-Fi, or video compression codecs. Because every compliant manufacturer must implement the underlying technical standard, SEP holders possess immense structural market power capable of blocking entire product lines via border customs injunctions unless constrained by licensing discipline.",
